{
  "slug": "ai-sync",
  "name": "Ai Sync",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Cross-platform AI agent synchronization. When you switch \n  between AI coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex,     \n  Aider, Cline, Windsurf, Copilot), ai-sync maintains a    \n  shared .ai-sync/ directory so the next agent picks up    \n  exactly where the last one left off — with full context  \n  of what was done, what's next, blockers, and build       \n  status. Features conflict detection, auto-progress       \n  tracking, session audit trails, and adapter files for 9  \n  tools.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **8 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `ai-sync-protocol` (This skill should be used when the project has a `.ai-sync/` directory, when the user mentions \"handoff\", \"switch…)\n- **Commands** (8): `handoff` (Write handoff state before switching to another AI agent), `sync-adapter` (Generate an adapter file for a specific AI tool — points the tool to .ai-sync/), `sync-diff` (Show what changed in the project since the last handoff), `sync-hooks` (Install or remove git hooks that auto-save .ai-sync/ context on every commit), `sync-init` (Bootstrap .ai-sync/ cross-agent synchronization in the current project), `sync-resume` (Resume work from last handoff — load context, apply state, and continue where the previous agent left off), `sync-status` (Show current .ai-sync/ state — progress, handoff status, and next steps), `sync-transfer` (Transfer session context from another AI tool into .ai-sync/ using continues)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ai-sync@claude-community` from `oreolion/ai-sync-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 2,
    "command": 8
  },
